3. Audio

   Every audio clip is a 30-second excerpt of a track from the Free Music
   Archive and keeps that track's own Creative Commons license. The tree info
   panel and the site's Credits page (web/public/data/<subset>/attribution.json)
   name the title, artist, license, and FMA page of every track.

   Only these licenses are used: CC BY, CC BY-SA, CC BY-NC, CC BY-NC-SA, CC0,
   and Public Domain. NoDerivatives and non-Creative-Commons tracks are left
   out.

   NonCommercial (NC) tracks must not be used commercially. This applies to
   anyone who runs, copies, or forks grove: the MIT License of the code does
   not grant any right to the audio. A commercial use needs either the NC
   tracks removed or permission from each rights holder.

4. Art

   Block textures, trees, and every other visual are generated in code by
   grove itself. No third-party images, models, or sounds are included.

